  "worked_solution": "To obtain the given graph, we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph to the right by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-1}.$\n\n- Translate the result up by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-1}+2.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/ea0e33e6af15954c3a58b873c82d7877bd3d82595feea8e51b273345309f3241.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=\\sqrt{x-1}+2.$",
